            <ArticleTitle>&quot;Bilateral knuckle&quot; technique and Stingray re-entry system for retrograde chronic total occlusion intervention.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>E37-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a novel technique for retrograde chronic total occlusion intervention, in which the lesion is crossed by forming and advancing a &quot;knuckle&quot; in both the antegrade and retrograde guidewire, followed by reentry in the true lumen by using the Stingray re-entry system.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
